    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "page_id": "topic-17-2-2",
    "page_path": "/explore/mining/metal-industries/copper/",
    "name": "Copper",
    "level": 3,
    "parent_path": "/explore/mining/metal-industries/",
    "entity_type": "category",
    "address": null,
    "phone": null,
    "email": null,
    "website": null,
    "logo": null,
    "contact_source_ids": [],
    "description": "Iran’s copper industry includes mining, concentration, smelting and refining, with important operations in Kerman Province and at Sungun. Ore, concentrate and refined copper represent different stages whose production figures require careful interpretation.",
    "tags": ["Copper", "Mineral processing", "Kerman", "Sarcheshmeh", "Refining"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-28T11:39:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T11:39:54Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Copper in Iran: Mines, Concentrates and Refined Metal",
      "description": "Understand Iran’s copper industry, its major mining centers, the routes from ore to cathode, and the distinctions behind production statistics."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "overview",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Following copper from mine to metal",
        "content": "Iran’s copper industry encompasses several activities that are often compressed into the phrase “copper production.” The US Geological Survey identifies Sarcheshmeh as a major ore-producing complex and discusses Sungun alongside newer processing developments in Kerman Province. Its industry review also identifies National Iranian Copper Industries Company, or NICICO, as an important sector participant. [s1]\n\nThose operations should be understood as parts of a material chain. Extracted ore contains copper-bearing minerals mixed with other rock. Concentration separates a richer material, while smelting and refining produce increasingly purified metal. A mine’s ore tonnage therefore cannot be compared directly with a refinery’s copper output. The first measures material handled; the second measures a product much closer to use in manufacturing. [s2][s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "processing",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Two routes to copper cathode",
        "content": "For sulfide ores, processing commonly begins with crushing and grinding. Flotation separates copper-bearing particles into a concentrate: reagents help selected mineral particles attach to bubbles and rise to the surface. Smelting and subsequent refining then transform this material into purified copper. The discarded mineral fraction and the metal-bearing concentrate are separate outputs of concentration. [s3]\n\nA different route uses leaching to dissolve copper, solvent extraction to separate and concentrate it in solution, and electrowinning to deposit metal using electricity. The appropriate route depends on the characteristics of the feedstock. These processes explain why a copper-industry table can contain separate entries for concentrate, smelter output, refinery output and electrowon metal without describing independent quantities that can all be summed. [s2][s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "process-diagram",
        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "Alternative routes from copper ore to refined metal",
        "content": "```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Copper-bearing ore\"] -->|\"Sulfide processing route\"| B[\"Crushing, grinding and flotation\"]\n  B -->|\"Produces concentrate\"| C[\"Smelting and converting\"]\n  C -->|\"Produces material for refining\"| D[\"Electrorefining\"]\n  D -->|\"Produces\"| E[\"Copper cathode\"]\n  A -->|\"Suitable leachable feedstock\"| F[\"Leaching and solvent extraction\"]\n  F -->|\"Supplies copper-bearing solution\"| G[\"Electrowinning\"]\n  G -->|\"Produces\"| E\n```",
        "summary": "The diagram explains alternative processing routes. It does not assign every stage to a particular Iranian facility or imply that all ore can use either route.",
        "as_of_date": null,
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "iranian-developments",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Reading expansion announcements",
        "content": "The USGS review reports completed processing developments at Dare Aloo and Darehzar in Kerman Province, as well as expansion at Sarcheshmeh. These are evidence of changes in processing infrastructure. They should not be treated automatically as equivalent increases in annual refined copper output. [s1]\n\nCapacity describes what equipment is designed to process or produce under specified conditions. Actual output depends on feedstock, operating time and performance across subsequent stages. Similarly, a revision to a deposit’s reported reserves is a statement about its assessed mineral inventory, rather than copper already extracted or available for immediate sale. These distinctions are essential when comparing mining announcements with production statistics. [s1][s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "uses-and-limits",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Connecting extraction with manufacturing",
        "content": "Refined copper enters semi-fabrication, where producers make wire rod, tubes, sheet and strip. Those materials then become electrical equipment, building components and other manufactured goods. Scrap can re-enter the chain at different stages, so primary production from mined material and secondary production from recycled material require separate definitions. [s4]\n\nFor Iran, a useful assessment must therefore connect mines with processing and downstream manufacturing. More ore handled does not by itself establish more saleable cathode, stronger domestic demand or improved environmental performance. This page retains the verified industrial outline while leaving the annual comparison open until reporting calendars and series coverage can be confirmed. [s1][s2][s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s4"]
      }
    ],
    "datasets": [],
